       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. The usual starting dose is 2.5 to 5 mg. A dose of 50 mg could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock, and it would be hard to reverse because amlodipine has a long half-life.\n\nCould you confirm which of these you meant?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the standard starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- **2.5 mg** by mouth once daily, a lower starting dose if the patient is frail or you want a more cautious start\n\nIf 50 mg is what you intended, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first. Once you confirm the dose, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
